WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.149
Week 29: Relative Clauses and Unknown Referents. define a requirement identify known and unknown people or things connect complex information

2
00:00:10.149 --> 00:00:17.844
Cultural lens. Job postings, housing searches, public notices, and precision in formal descriptions.

3
00:00:17.844 --> 00:00:29.937
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:29.937 --> 00:00:41.731
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:41.731 --> 00:00:50.773
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:50.773 --> 00:01:20.359
Model language. Buscamos a alguien que tenga experiencia. — We are looking for someone who has experience. Conozco a la persona que dirige el proyecto. — I know the person who directs the project. Necesito un lugar que esté cerca del metro. — I need a place that is near the subway. Eso es lo que me preocupa. — That is what worries me. La autora, cuyo libro ganó el premio, dará una charla. — The author whose book won the prize will give a talk.

7
00:01:20.359 --> 00:01:30.257
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
